"The postoperative pathology reveals a Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2) diagnosis with pathological stage pT3a. Adverse findings include positive surgical margins, although the seminal vesicles were not invaded, and lymphovascular invasion was absent. The biopsy identified a Gleason 3+3 (ISUP grade group 1) pattern. The absence of documented nodal sampling means that the pNx status does not establish node-negative disease, which widens the uncertainty regarding regional spread. Countervailing findings include the absence of lymphovascular invasion and seminal vesicle invasion. Postoperative PSA is not recorded, so biochemical recurrence cannot be assessed. Information regarding postoperative PSA and its trajectory is crucial for revising the prognosis. Missing nodal sampling limits staging information. The fixed estimated horizon is 66.41 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 43.16–89.65 months; its coverage has not been validated."
